# Lets the status-box service unmount the card and shut the Pi down
# without a password prompt -- it runs unprivileged (see
# analyze-and-backup-status.service's User=), and there's no TTY under
# systemd for sudo to prompt on anyway, so without this the safe-shutdown
# button would just silently fail both commands.
#
# Scoped to exactly the two commands it needs, not blanket passwordless
# sudo, so a bug in pi_status_box.py can't do anything else as root.
#
# Installed by deploy/install.sh to /etc/sudoers.d/ -- do not edit that
# copy directly, edit this source file and re-run install.sh instead.

__PROJECT_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/umount, /sbin/shutdown, /usr/sbin/shutdown
